1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,010
Graham Tolliver had saved his company, and
everybody had told him so.

2
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:18,715
The licence had cut his run time to thirty-one
minutes. The trade press had called him

3
00:00:18,735 --> 00:00:24,411
decisive. His lender had stopped calling on Fridays.
And every quarter, nine million dollars

4
00:00:24,431 --> 00:00:29,798
left his accounts and went to Wilmington, and four
per cent of every panel he sold went

5
00:00:29,818 --> 00:00:35,186
with it, and at the end of the first quarter his
chief financial officer put a slide in

6
00:00:35,206 --> 00:00:40,511
front of him showing the five-year projection, which
was a straight line going down at

7
00:00:40,531 --> 00:00:41,439
a polite angle.

8
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:46,140
It is one thing to lose. It is another
thing entirely to be kept.

9
00:00:46,539 --> 00:00:52,623
On the sixth of April, Tolliver stopped negotiating
with Albert Wesker and started fighting

10
00:00:52,643 --> 00:00:58,324
him, and the narrator would like to say, before any
of this begins, that he was not a

11
00:00:58,344 --> 00:01:04,093
fool. He was a competent chief executive with eleven
hundred employees who depended on

12
00:01:04,113 --> 00:01:08,519
him, and every single thing he tried was
the correct thing to try.

13
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:11,310
He tried three moves in eleven days.

14
00:01:11,709 --> 00:01:17,863
The first was legal: a suit in the District of
Delaware alleging that the archive licence

15
00:01:17,883 --> 00:01:23,968
Verdant Axis had bought in 2019 had been exclusive in
substance if not in form, and that

16
00:01:23,988 --> 00:01:30,142
Umbrella's entire instrument line was built on
material it had no right to commercialise.

17
00:01:30,162 --> 00:01:36,108
It was a stretch. It was also the kind of stretch
that takes two years and twenty-nine

18
00:01:36,128 --> 00:01:38,119
million dollars to unstretch.

19
00:01:38,519 --> 00:01:44,828
The second was people: offers to Evelyn Marsh and
to two of Voss's process engineers,

20
00:01:44,848 --> 00:01:50,190
at two and a half times their salaries, with
signing bonuses and titles.

21
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:56,386
The third was quieter. He hired a firm in Virginia —
the kind with a two-word name and

22
00:01:56,406 --> 00:02:02,337
no website — to find out what was in the building in
Wilmington. What he said, on a call

23
00:02:02,357 --> 00:02:08,423
that was later read into evidence in a hearing that
went nowhere, was: *I don't want dirt.

24
00:02:08,443 --> 00:02:14,240
I want to know how they did it in ninety days.
Because nobody does it in ninety days.*

25
00:02:14,639 --> 00:02:17,669
And that, of the three, was the
one that ended him.

26
00:02:18,069 --> 00:02:20,319
Wesker did not defend.

27
00:02:20,719 --> 00:02:26,930
This is the thing that everyone who ever fought him got
wrong, at every scale, for sixty-five

28
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:33,161
years, right up to a hive at the edge of a dead system:
they expected a defence, and prepared

29
00:02:33,181 --> 00:02:39,057
for a defence, and what arrived instead was a man who
had already decided that the fight

30
00:02:39,077 --> 00:02:41,670
was a distraction from the acquisition.

31
00:02:42,189 --> 00:02:46,964
(flat) The complaint is served. Our counsel believes
we would win at summary judgment,

32
00:02:46,984 --> 00:02:48,859
but not before March of next year.

33
00:02:49,259 --> 00:02:51,700
Don't answer it yet. What does
their paper look like?

34
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:56,781
Two hundred and twenty-nine million in senior debt
held by a syndicate. Lead is Merrick

35
00:02:56,801 --> 00:03:01,374
Trust — a regional lender, conservative, and
unhappy. They wrote the facility in 2023

36
00:03:01,394 --> 00:03:06,075
when the panel was still the best in the market.
There is a covenant tested on trailing

37
00:03:06,095 --> 00:03:10,991
twelve-month revenue, and a change-of-control clause,
and a provision permitting assignment

38
00:03:11,011 --> 00:03:12,990
of the debt without borrower consent.

39
00:03:13,390 --> 00:03:17,178
They may sell his loan to anyone at all,
and he cannot stop them.

40
00:03:17,579 --> 00:03:18,549
They may.

41
00:03:18,949 --> 00:03:19,694
What would it take?

42
00:03:20,096 --> 00:03:24,829
The syndicate would part with the paper at
ninety-one cents. A hundred and ninety-two

43
00:03:24,849 --> 00:03:27,346
million dollars. We have
thirty-nine in cash.

44
00:03:27,746 --> 00:03:30,776
Wesker looked at the number for a moment.

45
00:03:31,295 --> 00:03:31,960
Catherine.

46
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:39,107
Catherine Adeyemi spent six days on the telephone
and did what nine years in London had

47
00:03:39,127 --> 00:03:39,807
been for.

48
00:03:40,206 --> 00:03:45,594
She did not raise a hundred and ninety-two million
dollars. She raised thirty — a bridge

49
00:03:45,614 --> 00:03:51,064
from a Boston credit fund against Umbrella's own
receivables and the Verdant Axis licence

50
00:03:51,084 --> 00:03:56,349
stream, which was the single most reliable cash flow
in the industry precisely because

51
00:03:56,369 --> 00:04:01,880
Tolliver could not stop paying it. Then she took the
thirty and bought the *lead* position

52
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:07,410
in the syndicate: not the whole loan, but the seat at
the table, with the amendment rights

53
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:08,516
that came with it.

54
00:04:09,037 --> 00:04:13,288
I want to be clear about what I've done, because when
this is over I will have to explain

55
00:04:13,308 --> 00:04:17,463
it to an auditor. We have not bought his company. We
have bought the right to be in the

56
00:04:17,483 --> 00:04:19,143
room when his company is discussed.

57
00:04:19,543 --> 00:04:21,125
That is all I have ever needed.

58
00:04:21,526 --> 00:04:25,988
There's something else. I met the Merrick people
twice. The second time, their credit

59
00:04:26,008 --> 00:04:30,733
officer asked me — carefully, the way you ask a
question you've been told to ask — whether

60
00:04:30,753 --> 00:04:35,479
Umbrella had any interest in acquiring Verdant Axis
outright. It was not an idle question.

61
00:04:35,499 --> 00:04:40,225
Someone at that bank has already run the numbers on
you as an owner and liked them better.

62
00:04:40,625 --> 00:04:47,054
Wesker was quiet for a moment, and the narrator would
like to note that this is the closest

63
00:04:47,074 --> 00:04:52,795
anybody came, in the whole of that first year, to
catching the machinery at work.

64
00:04:53,314 --> 00:04:54,270
Did they say why?

65
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:56,473
They said your paper is clean.

66
00:04:56,872 --> 00:04:57,561
Yes. It is.

67
00:04:57,961 --> 00:05:01,441
On the night of the thirteenth, four
men came over the wall.

68
00:05:01,841 --> 00:05:07,179
They were not criminals, particularly. Two were
ex-military, one was a former Delaware

69
00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:12,538
state trooper, and the fourth carried a camera with
a low-light sensor worth more than

70
00:05:12,558 --> 00:05:18,022
the car they had arrived in. Their instructions were
to photograph the loading dock, the

71
00:05:18,042 --> 00:05:23,443
transformer yard, and anything on the south side of
the building that looked newer than

72
00:05:23,463 --> 00:05:25,251
the paperwork said it should.

73
00:05:25,651 --> 00:05:30,831
They came over the wall at one fifty. They were
on the ground for eleven seconds.

74
00:05:31,230 --> 00:05:36,869
Hale was standing on the service road when they
landed. Not running towards it — standing

75
00:05:36,889 --> 00:05:42,591
on it, with his hands at his sides, having been in
that exact spot since one thirty-eight.

76
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:47,001
(flat) This is private property. You will
leave the way you came.

77
00:05:47,401 --> 00:05:53,533
The man with the camera — his name was Wendell Tarr,
and he is the only one of the four

78
00:05:53,553 --> 00:05:59,969
who ever spoke about it on the record — later
described what happened next in a deposition,

79
00:05:59,989 --> 00:06:04,071
and then in a psychiatrist's office,
and then never again.

80
00:06:04,471 --> 00:06:10,656
There was a man at the far end of the road, about
forty metres away, in a long black coat.

81
00:06:10,676 --> 00:06:13,621
Tarr saw him clearly. He
raised the camera.

82
00:06:14,021 --> 00:06:19,905
Between the moment the shutter opened and the moment
it closed — which, at the setting

83
00:06:19,925 --> 00:06:25,947
he was using, was one one-hundred-and-sixtieth of a
second — the man was no longer forty

84
00:06:25,967 --> 00:06:26,771
metres away.

85
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:32,893
He was standing beside Wendell Tarr, close enough to
touch, with one gloved hand resting

86
00:06:32,913 --> 00:06:38,440
on the top of the camera, looking at him through a
pair of black glasses in the dark.

87
00:06:39,346 --> 00:06:41,532
That is an excellent lens. What is it for?

88
00:06:41,932 --> 00:06:47,456
Tarr could not answer. One of the others — the
trooper — went for something at his waist,

89
00:06:47,476 --> 00:06:52,750
and Hale's hand closed over his wrist, and that was
the whole of the violence: a hand

90
00:06:52,770 --> 00:06:54,682
on a wrist, which stayed there.

91
00:06:55,201 --> 00:06:58,096
I am going to tell you four things, and then
you are going to go home.

92
00:06:58,375 --> 00:07:03,071
The first is that nobody here is going to hurt you.
The second is that there is nothing

93
00:07:03,091 --> 00:07:07,732
on this campus that would interest your client, and
he knows it, or he would have sent

94
00:07:07,752 --> 00:07:12,502
people he was willing to lose. The third is that Mr.
Tolliver is paying you a great deal

95
00:07:12,522 --> 00:07:17,163
of money out of a company that will not exist in
ninety days, so I would encourage you

96
00:07:17,183 --> 00:07:18,463
to invoice him promptly.

97
00:07:18,865 --> 00:07:20,875
He lifted his hand off the camera.

98
00:07:21,394 --> 00:07:26,169
And the fourth is that you will find, when you try
to describe this, that the sentence

99
00:07:26,189 --> 00:07:30,907
does not survive being spoken aloud. Try it in the
car. You will get about half of it

100
00:07:30,927 --> 00:07:34,865
out, and then you will hear yourself, and
you will stop. Everyone does.

101
00:07:35,266 --> 00:07:40,894
They went back over the wall. The memory card was not
taken from them — that is the part

102
00:07:40,914 --> 00:07:46,477
that stayed with Tarr the longest. Nobody took the
card. They got to the car and looked

103
00:07:46,497 --> 00:07:52,061
at the frame, and the frame showed an empty road
with a smear of black at the left-hand

104
00:07:52,081 --> 00:07:55,656
edge, which any competent person
would call motion blur.

105
00:07:56,055 --> 00:08:01,206
Three of the four quit the firm inside a month.
Wendell Tarr kept the photograph.

106
00:08:02,355 --> 00:08:11,204
Acting with intelligence. Intrusion resolved without
injury, arrest or record. Four witnesses.

107
00:08:11,224 --> 00:08:16,205
Zero credible accounts produced.
Six thousand Points.

108
00:08:16,795 --> 00:08:20,185
From somewhere behind his eyes, the
passenger spoke.

109
00:08:20,704 --> 00:08:22,112
You let them go.

110
00:08:22,512 --> 00:08:27,501
I let them *carry* it. Four men who cannot repeat
what they saw, working in an industry

111
00:08:27,521 --> 00:08:32,509
of three hundred people who all drink together. By
June every private intelligence firm

112
00:08:32,529 --> 00:08:37,632
on this coast will have heard a story they do not
believe about a building in Wilmington,

113
00:08:37,652 --> 00:08:41,776
and every one of them will quote a price for
it that no client will pay.

114
00:08:42,177 --> 00:08:44,624
You have made yourself a rumour.

115
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:49,555
I have made myself an *expensive* rumour. It is the
cheapest security money can buy.

116
00:08:49,955 --> 00:08:55,141
The board met at two o'clock on the fourth of May to
consider a proposal from its lead

117
00:08:55,161 --> 00:08:55,565
lender.

118
00:08:55,965 --> 00:09:01,913
The proposal was simple. Merrick Trust and the
syndicate would support a recapitalisation

119
00:09:01,933 --> 00:09:07,680
in which Umbrella Life Sciences would acquire
Verdant Axis Therapeutics for a dollar a

120
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:13,448
share, assume the debt, retain the workforce, and
drop the litigation. The alternative

121
00:09:13,468 --> 00:09:17,673
was to test the covenant in July, which
the company would fail.

122
00:09:18,072 --> 00:09:24,016
Nine directors. They had been arguing for fifty
minutes when the door at the end of the

123
00:09:24,036 --> 00:09:30,049
room opened and Wesker came in alone, twenty minutes
after he had been due, and sat down

124
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:32,723
in the empty chair without apologising.

125
00:09:33,123 --> 00:09:38,723
He let them finish. That is the thing that the two
surviving directors both mentioned,

126
00:09:38,743 --> 00:09:44,474
independently, years apart, to two different people.
He let them finish arguing, for six

127
00:09:44,494 --> 00:09:47,873
more minutes, about a company he
had already bought.

128
00:09:48,393 --> 00:09:50,203
You've had this planned since November.

129
00:09:50,602 --> 00:09:52,962
Since the twelfth of November, yes.

130
00:09:53,363 --> 00:09:56,853
You gave me a licence so I'd survive long
enough to be worth taking.

131
00:09:57,253 --> 00:10:01,744
I gave you a licence so that you would spend six
months proving, in public, with audited

132
00:10:01,764 --> 00:10:06,306
numbers, that my chemistry is worth nine million a
quarter to a competitor. You have been

133
00:10:06,326 --> 00:10:10,561
my best salesman since Christmas. It would have
been discourteous to interrupt you.

134
00:10:10,961 --> 00:10:16,673
Tolliver stood up. He was not a small man, and he
had been a serious person for thirty

135
00:10:16,693 --> 00:10:22,538
years, and the narrator would like to record that
what he said next was the truest thing

136
00:10:22,558 --> 00:10:24,205
anyone said in that room.

137
00:10:24,724 --> 00:10:28,825
What *are* you? Nobody moves like this. Nobody
builds a plant in a night — I have the

138
00:10:28,845 --> 00:10:33,092
aerial photographs, I have *satellite*, I have a
picture of that lot from 2023 and there

139
00:10:33,112 --> 00:10:36,874
is a plant in it and I stood on that lot in 2023
and there was nothing there —

140
00:10:37,274 --> 00:10:40,574
And Albert Wesker took off the sunglasses.

141
00:10:41,524 --> 00:10:47,432
There is no record of what Graham Tolliver saw. The
minutes note only that the chief executive

142
00:10:47,452 --> 00:10:52,793
sat down. The two directors who spoke about it
afterwards both said the same thing in

143
00:10:52,813 --> 00:10:58,153
slightly different words: that the room went very
quiet, and that Tolliver's hand was

144
00:10:58,173 --> 00:11:03,514
shaking against the table, and that neither of them
looked directly at the man in the

145
00:11:03,534 --> 00:11:06,793
chair for the remaining four
minutes of the meeting.

146
00:11:07,193 --> 00:11:09,024
The vote was nine to nothing.

147
00:11:09,423 --> 00:11:12,183
He put the glasses back on
before he stood up.

148
00:11:12,703 --> 00:11:17,161
Mr. Tolliver. Your contract has twelve months to
run and I intend to honour it. There

149
00:11:17,181 --> 00:11:21,850
is an office for you in Trenton and a title with the
word *emeritus* in it. You will keep

150
00:11:21,870 --> 00:11:26,539
your health plan and your pension and your parking
space, and you will never make another

151
00:11:26,559 --> 00:11:28,066
decision as long as you live.

152
00:11:28,466 --> 00:11:29,157
Why?

153
00:11:29,557 --> 00:11:33,927
Because you fought me competently, and because in four
months, when people ask what happens

154
00:11:33,947 --> 00:11:38,027
to men who fight me, I would like the answer to be
*nothing interesting*. It is a far

155
00:11:38,047 --> 00:11:40,102
more frightening answer than
the other one.

156
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:49,465
Rival absorbed entire. Verdant Axis Therapeutics,
acquired. One thousand one hundred and

157
00:11:49,485 --> 00:11:57,628
eight staff. Three facilities. Sixty-one patents.
Forty thousand Points. Level twelve.

158
00:11:58,846 --> 00:12:06,460
Main mission, tier two: all requirements complete.
Tier advancement will resolve at the

159
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:08,128
next reward window.

160
00:12:08,719 --> 00:12:14,727
The sign came down the same night. Wesker had
specified it: not in the morning, when the

161
00:12:14,747 --> 00:12:20,755
staff would gather and photograph it and feel
something, but at half past nine at night,

162
00:12:20,775 --> 00:12:23,769
with two men and a lift and
nobody watching.

163
00:12:24,168 --> 00:12:29,904
In the morning there was simply a crimson iris on a
building in Trenton, and eleven hundred

164
00:12:29,924 --> 00:12:35,343
people arriving at work for a company whose name had
changed while they slept, which —

165
00:12:35,363 --> 00:12:40,846
by the standards of what had happened to the three
hundred and thirteen in Newark — was

166
00:12:40,866 --> 00:12:43,629
an unusually gentle thing to do
to a person.

167
00:12:44,028 --> 00:12:46,818
He stood in the car park for a
while afterwards.

168
00:12:47,219 --> 00:12:50,389
The voice in his skull chose that
moment to arrive.

169
00:12:50,908 --> 00:12:52,447
Eleven hundred more.

170
00:12:52,846 --> 00:12:58,514
Eleven hundred who can quit, complain, sue, or talk
to a journalist. It is the largest

171
00:12:58,534 --> 00:13:01,359
liability I have ever
voluntarily acquired.

172
00:13:01,759 --> 00:13:03,539
And yet you are pleased.

173
00:13:03,938 --> 00:13:09,106
I am pleased because eight months ago I was a man in
a chair with nine thousand Points

174
00:13:09,126 --> 00:13:14,716
and a laboratory full of nothing, and tomorrow morning
I will own the second-best diagnostics

175
00:13:14,736 --> 00:13:17,490
company on this continent as
well as the best.

176
00:13:17,890 --> 00:13:19,961
He looked up at the iris on the wall.

177
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:25,059
And because tomorrow the System pays me for it, and
I have decided what I am going to

178
00:13:25,079 --> 00:13:25,708
spend it on.
